1
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:11,750
I'm traveling through a tunnel right now on a train that's going 200 kilometers an hour.

2
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:17,890
And above me, there's two and a half kilometers of pure rock.

3
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,530
That's a mile and a half of nothing but mountain.

4
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:25,400
This tunnel is 57 kilometers long.

5
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,510
It's 35 miles.

6
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:28,610
It's the longest on the planet.

7
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:38,300
A few months ago,

8
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,060
I asked the people

9
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:40,300
who run Switzerland's trains

10
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,620
if they would let me spend a week doing nothing

11
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:43,980
but living on their trains

12
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:48,280
so I could stress test this world -famous system to see how hard I

13
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:49,150
could push its limits.

14
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,900
And they gave me free reign.

15
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:52,760
They gave me a ticket

16
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,780
that allows me to go on any train,

17
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:58,870
even first class, which I didn't really discover until halfway through my trip.

18
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,320
And in this moment,

19
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,240
I'm in the middle of a race to see

20
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:05,400
if I can step foot on all 26 Swiss regions,

21
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:10,650
or cantons, in under 24 hours, but only using public transportation.

22
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:19,720
And along the way,

23
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:24,240
locals who responded to my call for stories on our community -driven journalism platform

24
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:26,150
are going to help me on this challenge.

25
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,270
We have a new plan.

26
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:35,030
I'm an American who doesn't really understand trains, I'm embarrassed to say.

27
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:37,890
My country is a country that loves cars.

28
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:40,820
So I'm here to try to understand what they've built,

29
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:41,700
how it works,

30
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:42,590
how it's designed,
